<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 03:48:37 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Americas</category><title>Miguel Angel Felix Gallardo, architect of Mexico’s drug trade, dies age 80</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-miguel-angel-felix-gallardo-mexican-drug-lord-dies</link><description>
Miguel Angel Felix Gallardo, a founder of Mexico’s Guadalajara cartel known as the “boss of bosses”, died in hospital on Sunday aged 80 after suffering multiple organ failure, Jalisco state’s security ministry said. Imprisoned since 1989, he had been transferred from prison to the hospital two days before his death.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3174496-e145-11f1-ae4a-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7JM9ZV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3174496-e145-11f1-ae4a-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7JM9ZV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a7fa30ac-e142-11f1-a70a-f7625ce3d617</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:48:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3174496-e145-11f1-ae4a-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7JM9ZV.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title><![CDATA['Record number of women elected' to US Congress & governorships across country in midterm elections]]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-record-number-of-women-elected-to-us-congress-governorships-across-country-in-midterm-elections</link><description>
Following the 2026 US midterm elections, Gavin Lee is pleased to welcome Politico Senior National Politics Reporter Lauren Fedor. She discusses the growing number of Democratic women elected to Congress and governorships, particularly mothers of young children. “There was a realisation across the map that perhaps moms were the best messenger for this,” she explains, pointing to voters' concerns about “the cost of living, affordability, how to make ends meet.”
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54cc366a-e10a-11f1-a9f0-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d8402e1a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54cc366a-e10a-11f1-a9f0-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d8402e1a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e754c538-e10a-11f1-85eb-35697e667a6f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:40:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Jensen Huang: The French Connection</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-jensen-huang-the-french-connection</link><description>
President Trump is heading to Asia in a few days time, and will meet President Putin and President Xi. There's likely to be one fewer tech giants at the table, Jensen Huang, newly resigned from Nvidia, over the suspected spy affair. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cb9bfd36-e05e-11f1-85e3-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/Jensen-Huang-000-36PC88T.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cb9bfd36-e05e-11f1-85e3-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/Jensen-Huang-000-36PC88T.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fad9359a-e05f-11f1-8600-8534dcd91768</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:03:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US probes nationwide flights stoppage as travel disruptions persist</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-probes-nationwide-flights-stoppage-as-travel-disruptions-persist</link><description>
US air travel is expected to return to normal this Sunday, following a nationwide ground stop Friday night that stranded hundreds of thousands of passengers and disrupted travel worldwide. The Trump administration blamed the incident on a botched replacement of old copper wire communication lines and said there was no evidence this was a cyberattack. The ground stop now raises questions about the country's aging infrastructure and lawmakers are calling for an investigation. Analysis by Philip Mann, aviation expert at Vector Strategic Consulting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f68e5f6c-e0fd-11f1-91ae-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T154335Z-516903887-RC2ONOAT735S-RTRMADP-3-USA-FAA-GROUND-STOP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f68e5f6c-e0fd-11f1-91ae-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T154335Z-516903887-RC2ONOAT735S-RTRMADP-3-USA-FAA-GROUND-STOP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4dfc6f98-e0fc-11f1-bdc8-ebeb331f4797</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:09:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Air travel issues persist in the US after nationwide ground stop</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/air-travel-issues-persist-in-the-us-after-nationwide-ground-stop</link><description>
After almost five hours of grounded flights in the US, flights have resumed. However, passengers are still waiting and wading through tough logistics to get to their destinations after massive delays and cancelled flights. Details by Simon Moritz.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ae37617a-e0ec-11f1-9eb5-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-080531-080704-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ae37617a-e0ec-11f1-9eb5-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-080531-080704-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b3965cd4-e0ec-11f1-abdc-0765d31dc03f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:12:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope laments poverty-stricken Inca communities as locals leave Peru</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-pope-laments-poverty-stricken-inca-communities-as-locals-leave-peru</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV on Sunday will traverse the length of Peru in what marks the penultimate day of his Latin American tour. The leader of the Catholic church – who underwent cancer surgery just a month ago – warned that Peru's remote Inca communities are under threat as poverty continues to drive locals out of their homeland in search of better futures.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/16926fb2-e0e8-11f1-b2bb-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T225151Z-1773168410-RC2XNOAB3YQ0-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/16926fb2-e0e8-11f1-b2bb-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T225151Z-1773168410-RC2XNOAB3YQ0-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8ccf0eaa-e0df-11f1-80f5-13c9a032c2ab</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:55:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/16926fb2-e0e8-11f1-b2bb-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T225151Z-1773168410-RC2XNOAB3YQ0-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg">© Yara Nardi, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>SpaceX makes rocketry history by recapturing massive reusable rocketship</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/spacex-makes-rocketry-history-by-recapturing-massive-reusable-rocketship</link><description>
After failing to catch a booster yesterday, SpaceX managed to recapture its massive reusable rocketship, "Starship" for the first time. Smaller previous models have successfully relanded but they require heavy legs and aren't fully reusable. Story by Daniel Quinlan.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c43ae00-e080-11f1-8286-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T213803Z-704233441-RC2XNOAR9QE8-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEX-STARSHIP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c43ae00-e080-11f1-8286-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T213803Z-704233441-RC2XNOAR9QE8-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEX-STARSHIP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">850a30bc-e0d7-11f1-ae22-9bc5bd8b1533</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:42:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope Leo urges stop to Amazon deforestation, demands justice for slain Indigenous leaders</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-pope-leo-visits-peru-s-high-altitude-cusco-testing-recovery-from-lung-cancer</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV travelled across Peru on Sunday to visit communities high in the Andes mountains and deep in the Amazon rainforest, testing his recovery from lung cancer surgery a month ago. The pontiff condemned the exploitation of the Amazon and urged Catholics to oppose "with perseverance" the deforestation and pollution caused by gold and oil production in the world's largest rainforest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9e3b2996-e137-11f1-9631-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T204810Z-1388210058-RC2KOOA0UH9W-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9e3b2996-e137-11f1-9631-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T204810Z-1388210058-RC2KOOA0UH9W-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">970a2b7e-e0b8-11f1-a6b0-a95900a5fd00</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:51:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9e3b2996-e137-11f1-9631-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T204810Z-1388210058-RC2KOOA0UH9W-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg">© Yara Nardi, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Elon Musk's SpaceX aborts booster recovery due to technical issues</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/elon-musk-s-spacex-aborts-booster-recovery-due-to-technical-issues</link><description>
Elon Musk's SpaceX is in the midst of a 15th test-flight of its Starship rocket. The company was hoping to pull off the first-ever "double catch" - with both the booster and the ship itself coming safely back down to earth. Instead, an unspecified problem forced the company to abort recovery of the booster, which was diverted from its return path and crashed down into the Gulf of Mexico. Analysis by journalist Frédéric Castel, based in Bosa Chica, Texas, USA.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ecebe06-e02b-11f1-b834-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-080810-081151-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ecebe06-e02b-11f1-b834-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-080810-081151-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">13e4d9b6-e02b-11f1-b702-954c0a5a64e9</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:33:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Washington divided over how to deal with fallout from the Nvidia case</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/washington-divided-over-how-to-deal-with-fallout-from-the-nvidia-case</link><description>
After the fall, the fallout. US government agencies are squabbling after AI leader Jensen Huang stepped down from chips giant Nvidia in disgrace. The Treasury says it wanted to blacklist a Singapore company at the heart of the scandal, but the Commerce Department didn't act. Megaspeed was run by suspected Chinese spy Alice Huang, who reportedly had an affair with Jensen Huang. Details by Peter O'Brien.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de9eb5ba-e025-11f1-b03b-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-120954-121129-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de9eb5ba-e025-11f1-b03b-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-120954-121129-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e3d9bc8c-e025-11f1-88eb-81d27dcb09cf</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:21:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US: What exactly caused the longest nationwide ground stop in 25 years?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-what-exactly-caused-the-longest-nationwide-ground-stop-in-25-years</link><description>
After a nearly five-hour ground stoppage, flights in the US have resumed. However, officials are warning that it will take days to recover from the ongoing delays related to the incident. Transport Secretary Sean Duffy explained the crisis was due to a failure in ageing telecommunications equipment. What exactly happened? Answers with FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Shirli Sitbon.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24754d74-e049-11f1-92be-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T154753Z-749061195-RC2ONOA67Q43-RTRMADP-3-USA-FAA-GROUND-STOP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24754d74-e049-11f1-92be-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T154753Z-749061195-RC2ONOA67Q43-RTRMADP-3-USA-FAA-GROUND-STOP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33b0d548-e043-11f1-9d13-0df17d5d03d9</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:35:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Transport Secretary asks Congress for $30 bn to upgrade aviation infrastructure</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-transport-secretary-asks-congress-for-30-bn-to-upgrade-aviation-infrastructure</link><description>
A failure in aging telecommunications equipment Friday forced a nationwide halt to departures from US airports. Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin says officials have found no evidence so far of a cyberattack, but that they're not ruling it out. Details by Jack Pownall.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fc695742-e040-11f1-8c71-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-150457-150644-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fc695742-e040-11f1-8c71-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-150457-150644-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">017d46a8-e041-11f1-b225-ad670de86b0f</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:32:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Copper wires blamed for US travel chaos as Trump asks Congress for money to overhaul system</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261114-copper-wires-to-blame-for-us-flight-disruption-says-trump-administration</link><description>
The Trump administration on Sunday pointed to aging infrastructure – specifically "a botched replacement of old copper wire communication lines" – as being responsible for the nationwide ground stop that snarled airline travel over the weekend. The president himself blamed the administration of his predecessor Joe Biden, in his first comments on the issue after a two-day silence.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77c62198-e0bb-11f1-bcbc-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2304620129.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77c62198-e0bb-11f1-bcbc-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2304620129.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">022e82f6-e041-11f1-b63f-df8f9f615923</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:35:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/77c62198-e0bb-11f1-bcbc-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2304620129.jpg">© Ryan Murphy, Getty Images via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>USA: All passengers survive after tanker hits docked river cruise ship in New Orleans</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/usa-all-passengers-survive-after-tanker-hits-docked-river-cruise-ship-in-new-orleans</link><description>
A portion of the Mississippi River remains closed after a collision between an oil tanker and a riverboat forced a chaotic river rescue in Louisiana. Story by Caitlin Brown.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/655a8158-e024-11f1-8b4c-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-120344-120524-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/655a8158-e024-11f1-8b4c-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-120344-120524-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a3a881c-e024-11f1-8dfc-13f9b3b00dd2</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:15:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Who are the 'street medics' showing up at protests around the world?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/who-are-the-street-medics-showing-up-at-protests-around-the-world</link><description>
From treating tear gas exposure to tending to injuries, street medics have become an increasingly common sight at protests all over the world. But who exactly are they and when did they start showing up at demonstrations? Story by Daniel Quinlan.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/764618c8-e025-11f1-878e-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d4ac3443.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/764618c8-e025-11f1-878e-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d4ac3443.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">405d92aa-e01f-11f1-9579-21782230ef7c</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:19:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Half a million people gather for an open-air mass by Pope Leo in Peru</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/half-a-million-people-gather-for-an-open-air-mass-by-pope-leo-in-peru</link><description>
Pope Leo said it was a "joy to be back" in his second home of Chiclayo, where he made his name as a bishop. This is the latest stop on his South America tour, the very tour that saw fears of cancellation after the Pope underwent surgery for lung cancer. Story by Vedika Bahl.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4004e80-e01c-11f1-be8e-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-13T214746Z-754212400-RC29NOA0KQRS-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4004e80-e01c-11f1-be8e-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-13T214746Z-754212400-RC29NOA0KQRS-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">81c01db6-e01b-11f1-9964-ef92d80b1580</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:17:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US nationwide flight ground stop: "Our routers got overloaded with data"</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-nationwide-flight-ground-stop-our-routers-got-overloaded-with-data</link><description>
On Friday, the Federal Aviation Administration issued a rare nationwide ground stop. More than 8,200 flights, or over 31% of those scheduled in the United States, were canceled. The ground stop lasted nearly five hours and was the longest in the country since September 11, 2001. Officials blamed outdated air traffic communications equipment, and said that there was no evidence of a cyber attack. The airspace is now reopened and flights have resumed.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3b36d9c-e011-11f1-b125-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-100114-100358-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3b36d9c-e011-11f1-b125-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261114-100114-100358-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8cfa494-e011-11f1-8d16-95a3d2c4d031</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:14:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US flights resume after nationwide ground stop lifted</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261114-us-flights-resume-after-nationwide-ground-stop-lifted-aviation</link><description>
The United States on Friday lifted an hours-long ground stop at the nation's airports, with top officials explaining that the disruption was not due to a cyberattack or a sweeping Microsoft outage. Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said that US airspace was now "opened up," and blamed "old hardware" for the travel chaos. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de33210e-dfd2-11f1-8675-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26317844187470.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de33210e-dfd2-11f1-8675-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26317844187470.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1a751d60-dfd4-11f1-94d0-4d5742533b4a</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:35:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de33210e-dfd2-11f1-8675-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26317844187470.jpg">© Tony Gutierrez, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Passengers face further disruption as US flights slowly resume after ground stop</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-us-air-travel-resumption-will-take-time-after-hours-long-stop</link><description>
While flights in the United States started resuming on Saturday following the longest nationwide ground stop in 25 years, more than 2,000 flights have been cancelled as airlines work to return to normal operations. Nearly 6,000 flights were cancelled on Friday, with the incident marking only the second time such an alert had been issued in US airspace since the 9/11 attacks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8070c46a-dff8-11f1-bbc8-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2304502550.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8070c46a-dff8-11f1-bbc8-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2304502550.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a182cba2-dfb3-11f1-a072-f7a26f71f35e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:43:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8070c46a-dff8-11f1-bbc8-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2304502550.jpg">© Finn Gomez, Getty Images via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US flight authority orders national ground stop over air traffic control 'communication issue'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-us-flight-authority-orders-national-ground-stop-over-air-traffic-control-communication-issue</link><description>
The US flight authority on Friday halted flights across the nation due to what US Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy said was a communication issue affecting the country's air traffic control centres.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0b9ef0bc-dfa8-11f1-84a6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-20T235835Z-122091610-RC297OANDGMD-RTRMADP-3-BOEING-737-MAX.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0b9ef0bc-dfa8-11f1-84a6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-20T235835Z-122091610-RC297OANDGMD-RTRMADP-3-BOEING-737-MAX.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">10458cac-dfa8-11f1-9cfb-8f5881cc457e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:27:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0b9ef0bc-dfa8-11f1-84a6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-20T235835Z-122091610-RC297OANDGMD-RTRMADP-3-BOEING-737-MAX.jpg">© Jason Redmond, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>The Nvidia affair: Are markets about to fall out of love with AI?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-the-nvidia-affair-are-markets-about-to-fall-out-of-love-with-ai</link><description>
Jensen Huang’s departure from Nvidia exposes the vulnerabilities behind the AI boom. As equities reel in response to his resignation following extramarital affairs, alleged Chinese espionage and a summons to testify before US lawmakers, questions mount over who is really in charge of tech and whether the immense capital riding on it can survive the turmoil. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f641d4de-deb5-11f1-8acd-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/6bb584644ef73cfa0c9ff3548f3f68f8f5d99d1a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f641d4de-deb5-11f1-8acd-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/6bb584644ef73cfa0c9ff3548f3f68f8f5d99d1a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">94d62524-df78-11f1-a89c-ffc2e87efde4</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:02:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f641d4de-deb5-11f1-8acd-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/6bb584644ef73cfa0c9ff3548f3f68f8f5d99d1a.jpg">© Patrick T. Fallon, AFP</source><dc:creator>Ella ARWYN JONES</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Haitian forces recapture national stadium after two years of gang control</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-haitian-forces-recapture-national-stadium-after-two-years-of-gang-control</link><description>
Haitian security forces regained control Thursday, November 12, of the country's main stadium that had been under gang control for two years, forcing the national football team to play elsewhere. The Haitian National Police said in a statement that it had taken "full control" of the venue with the Task Force, a private security group serving the government, after which it left the stadium under the guard of Salvadoran soldiers.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0f629408-df6f-11f1-8eb6-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T233346Z-704608318-RC26MOAZMZ8G-RTRMADP-3-HAITI-VIOLENCE-EL-SALVADOR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0f629408-df6f-11f1-8eb6-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T233346Z-704608318-RC26MOAZMZ8G-RTRMADP-3-HAITI-VIOLENCE-EL-SALVADOR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">100533b8-df6d-11f1-b73a-ab85f13a3bba</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:09:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Devastated wasteland': Haitian security forces regain control of stadium from gangs</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-devastated-wasteland-haitian-security-forces-regain-control-of-stadium-from-gangs</link><description>
Haitian security forces said they have regained control of the country's main stadium, wresting it back from the gangs that have been using it for the past two years. They were assisted by the Task Force, a private security group serving the government. The stadium is now under the guard of Salvadoran soldiers. FRANCE 24's senior reporter Catherine Norris Trent, who has covered Haiti extensively, said re-taking the stadium would be a significant step in an area of the city that had been a "devastated wasteland".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5666bbe6-df69-11f1-b17b-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-be5b4980.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5666bbe6-df69-11f1-b17b-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-be5b4980.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9a040ef4-df68-11f1-8be3-2719fe6ac779</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:37:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Scoop</category><title>Midterms: What does the 'blue tsunami' mean for US media?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261113-what-does-the-blue-tsunami-mean-for-us-media</link><description>
This week, FRANCE 24's media show Scoop looks at the impact of the midterm elections in the United States. While the results are being reckoned with by Republicans and celebrated by Democrats, what does it all mean for the press? Some media analysts wonder whether certain outlets, particularly ones accused of being cosy with the Trump administration, will change their tone. Our guest this week is International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/41cc5bba-dd7e-11f1-a5e8-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26294694444631.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/41cc5bba-dd7e-11f1-a5e8-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26294694444631.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5f0ee8a0-df63-11f1-b764-c56daffef55b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:22:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>William HILDERBRANDT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>The scourge of femicide in Mexico: Impunity reigns in state of Morelos</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261113-the-scourge-of-femicide-in-mexico-impunity-reigns-in-state-of-morelos</link><description>
When Claudia Sheinbaum became Mexico's first female president in 2024, she pledged to tackle violence against women. And while femicides have fallen since she took office, the numbers remain alarming, with around 520 murders so far this year. In the small state of Morelos, just outside the capital Mexico City, four female students have been murdered since January, including a Spanish woman on an exchange programme. The state has one of the highest femicide rates in the country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd222762-deb1-11f1-a6ae-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-FREEZE-MEXICO-FEMICIDES-BAIN-Lauren.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd222762-deb1-11f1-a6ae-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-FREEZE-MEXICO-FEMICIDES-BAIN-Lauren.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">66e3a284-deb2-11f1-aafd-c12e2ce36d20</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:38:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Quentin DUVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Peruvians flock to see Pope Leo XIV in city he served as bishop</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-peruvians-flock-to-see-pope-leo-xiv-in-city-he-served-as-bishop</link><description>
Crowds in Peru's northern city of Chiclayo gathered early on Friday, November 13, ​ahead of ‌Pope Leo's arrival for the centerpiece event of his 12-day South America tour, an outdoor ⁠Mass with the people who called him their bishop for eight years. He declared on November 11 that the country where he served as a missionary for about 20 years was his homeland.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/662d1666-df4f-11f1-9644-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-68eec3bc.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/662d1666-df4f-11f1-9644-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-68eec3bc.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">91d46e50-df4e-11f1-8c57-b3c662a6e18d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:55:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope Leo XIV meets clerical abuse victims in Peru, says Church must make 'amends'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-pope-leo-xiv-meets-abuse-victims-in-peru-says-church-must-make-amends</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV met six victims of clerical abuse in Peru on Thursday, including people linked to the disbanded group Sodalitium Christianae Vitae. The US-born pontiff also urged the Catholic Church to make amends to survivors and strengthen protections against abuse as he returned to the country where he served as a missionary and bishop for nearly two decades.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/74ed1b6a-ded2-11f1-a1e7-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/e508fb7b23659b4d2a2f46189ca72db15c5d2dbc.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/74ed1b6a-ded2-11f1-a1e7-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/e508fb7b23659b4d2a2f46189ca72db15c5d2dbc.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1d58660c-df0e-11f1-9817-c7a27ad55a29</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:58:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/74ed1b6a-ded2-11f1-a1e7-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/e508fb7b23659b4d2a2f46189ca72db15c5d2dbc.jpg">© Tiziana Fabi, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Haitian police retake national stadium after two years of gang control</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261113-haitian-police-retake-national-stadium-from-gangs-after-two-years</link><description>
Haitian security forces regained control of the country's main football stadium Thursday after two years under gang control, with Salvadoran troops taking over security at the venue. El Salvador deployed 2,000 soldiers to Haiti following an ambush that left four of its troops missing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3dd13174-df00-11f1-9b27-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T233347Z-933808832-RC24MOADXTJ7-RTRMADP-3-HAITI-VIOLENCE-EL-SALVADOR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3dd13174-df00-11f1-9b27-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T233347Z-933808832-RC24MOADXTJ7-RTRMADP-3-HAITI-VIOLENCE-EL-SALVADOR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">22c04a54-df06-11f1-97b0-1908cbabb3a5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:01:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3dd13174-df00-11f1-9b27-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T233347Z-933808832-RC24MOADXTJ7-RTRMADP-3-HAITI-VIOLENCE-EL-SALVADOR.jpg">© Fildor Pq Egeder, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>'Peruvian pope' Leo XIV comes home to a country that shaped his life and faith through 'hardship'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261112-peruvian-pope-leo-xiv-comes-home-to-a-country-that-shaped-his-life-and-faith-through-hardship</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Victor Casallo, Director of the Department of Philosophical and Theological Studies at Antonio Ruiz de Montoya University. Can a pope shaped by Peru's history of political violence, social inequality and religious activism help a deeply polarised nation heal and rediscover the possibility of dialogue? "We tend to see the other person not as someone who holds a different opinion, but as an enemy." Casallo argues that with Pope Leo, the first American-born pontiff's identity cannot be understood through his Chicago origins alone.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40404e94-df92-11f1-816b-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-687331a7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40404e94-df92-11f1-816b-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-687331a7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6936791e-def1-11f1-96ef-bf46bbbd6e25</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:33:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>New York building collapse kills eight, including two children</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-eight-killed-including-two-children-in-new-york-building-collapse</link><description>
Eight people, including two children, were killed when a residential building collapsed into an adjacent construction site in Brooklyn on Wednesday. Firefighters spent hours searching the rubble overnight before declaring the operation over on Thursday as authorities launched an investigation into the disaster.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/82abc90a-deea-11f1-8c96-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316296072440.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/82abc90a-deea-11f1-8c96-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316296072440.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">907174c0-deec-11f1-88b2-7b6870e6d6ea</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:58:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/82abc90a-deea-11f1-8c96-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316296072440.jpg">© Ryan Murphy, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
